# Secrets for {{ app }} in UAT

Sealed secrets go in this folder. Each one can only be opened by the cluster, and only as
that Secret name in namespace `{{ app }}-uat`. Values are piped into the sealing script and
never appear on a command line, on screen or in Git. Run from the root of GitOps-Repo.

| Secret | Keys | Who provides the values |
|---|---|---|
| `ghcr-pull` | `.dockerconfigjson` | Platform team (registry read token) |
{%- if backend != 'not-needed' %}
| `backend-secrets` | `JWT_SECRET`{% if needs_redis %}, `REDIS_URL`{% endif %} and every other secret the backend reads | The app's secret owners (readiness rule A18) |
{%- endif %}

```sh
# Registry pull secret (a token with ONLY read:packages)
read -rsp 'token: ' t; echo
printf '.dockerconfigjson={"auths":{"ghcr.io":{"auth":"%s"}}}\n' "$(printf '%s' "bot:$t" | base64 -w0)" \
  | ./scripts/seal-secret.sh {{ app }} uat ghcr-pull kubernetes.io/dockerconfigjson
{% if backend != 'not-needed' %}
# Backend secrets (one KEY=VALUE per line; add every variable the app reads)
printf 'JWT_SECRET=%s\n' "$(openssl rand -hex 32)" \
  | ./scripts/seal-secret.sh {{ app }} uat backend-secrets
{% endif %}
```
{% if needs_postgres %}
The database and its role (`{{ app }}_uat`) are declared in `../values.yaml`
(`database.managed`) and created by the platform's Crossplane provider; the
generated password reaches the pods as `DATABASE_URL`. Nothing to request,
nothing to seal.
{% endif %}
{% if needs_kafka %}
The Kafka user (`{{ app }}_uat`, fenced to `uat.{{ app }}.*`) and the topics are
declared in `../values.yaml` (`kafka.managed`) and created by the platform's
Crossplane provider; the pods get `KAFKA_USERNAME`, `KAFKA_PASSWORD`,
`KAFKA_BROKERS` and `KAFKA_TOPIC_PREFIX` from it.
{% endif %}
{% if needs_redis %}
Lab services (`scripts/lab-services.sh`) create the Redis user from
`{{ app | upper | replace('-', '_') }}_UAT_REDIS_PASSWORD` in team-secrets. At RSSB this is a
request to the Redis owners (infra-ops form).
{%- endif %}

Delete this file once the secrets are sealed, or keep it as the inventory.
